For example:
Two patients with metabolic syndrome may differ in the relative contribution of inflammatory, mitochondrial, and neuroendocrine axes.
In autoimmune conditions, variations in barrier integrity, microbiome composition, and immune regulation axes can produce distinct clinical presentations.
In neurodegenerative diseases, interactions between oxidative stress, mitochondrial dysfunction, and protein clearance axes determine disease trajectory.
By analyzing these patterns, clinicians can move beyond categorical diagnosis to personalized network profiling, identifying the specific axes that require intervention.
