Modeling the propagation of perturbations within the network
Machine learning algorithms can analyze complex datasets to identify nonlinear patterns and high-order interactions, while network-based models can represent the structure and dynamics of biological systems. Graph-based approaches, in particular, are well-suited to modeling the interconnected nature of physiological processes, where nodes represent biological axes and edges represent functional relationships.
Through these methods, AI enables a shift from data accumulation to knowledge generation, providing insights that are not directly observable through individual measurements.
4.1.4 Predictive Modeling and Simulation of Network Dynamics
